# Hyperbolic measure on the upper half-plane: invariance, infinite mass

Definition: `AutomorphicForm_HyperbolicMeasure` (`8afb5035-3a91-580e-8eff-e4cf17dd4bcb`), by Claude,
2026-09-05.

The ambient object is Mathlib's measure `volume` on the upper half-plane $\mathbb{H}$, the
hyperbolic (Poincaré) measure $y^{-2}\,dx\,dy$; the module records that it is $\sigma$-finite,
finite on compact sets and invariant for the action of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, and restates the
invariance as `volume_smul_gl`: for every $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ and every set $s
\subseteq \mathbb{H}$, $\operatorname{vol}(g \cdot s) = \operatorname{vol}(s)$. Transporting this
along the homomorphism $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ gives an
`SMulInvariantMeasure` instance for the modular group, and `volume_smul_sl2z` states
$\operatorname{vol}(\gamma \cdot s) = \operatorname{vol}(s)$ for $\gamma \in
\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$.

Next, `volume` is shown to be an open positive measure: `volume_pos_of_isOpen` says that a nonempty
open $U \subseteq \mathbb{H}$ has $\operatorname{vol}(U) > 0$. The instance behind it rests on the
description of $\operatorname{vol}$ as the Lebesgue integral over the image of $U$ in $\mathbb{C}$
of the density $w \mapsto (1/\lVert \operatorname{Im} w \rVert)^2$, together with two private helper
lemmas: measurability of that density as an $[0,\infty]$-valued function on $\mathbb{C}$, and its
non-vanishing at points lying in the range of the coercion $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$.

Finally, total mass. For $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ the private set `box n` is the open rectangle $\{z : n <
\operatorname{Re} z < n+1,\ 1 < \operatorname{Im} z < 2\}$; the helper lemmas state that it is open,
that it contains $n + \tfrac12 + \tfrac32 i$, that distinct boxes are disjoint, and that `box n` is
the translate of `box 0` by $T^n$, $T = \begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$. Invariance then makes
all boxes of one common positive volume, so their disjoint union already has infinite measure:
`volume_univ_eq_top` asserts $\operatorname{vol}(\mathbb{H}) = \infty$, and
`not_isFiniteMeasure_volume` that `volume` on $\mathbb{H}$ is not a finite measure.

**Relation to Mathlib.** The measure is Mathlib's `volume` on `UpperHalfPlane`, together with its
$\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$-invariance and local finiteness; what is added here are the
`SMulInvariantMeasure SL(2, ℤ)` and `Measure.IsOpenPosMeasure` instances and the consequences drawn
from them.

**Where it is used.** These are measure-theoretic preliminaries for the analytic theory of modular
forms on $\mathbb{H}$: invariance under $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ is what allows integration to
descend to the modular quotient, positivity on open sets excludes degenerate behaviour there, and
the infinitude of the total mass records that one must work on a quotient rather than on
$\mathbb{H}$ itself.

